# Day 37 - Subarray Sum Equals K

## Problem Statement
Given an integer array `nums` and an integer `k`, return the total number of contiguous subarrays whose sum is equal to `k`.

A subarray is a contiguous non-empty sequence of elements within an array.

## Code

class Solution {
public:
    int subarraySum(vector<int>& arr, int k) {
        unordered_map<int, int> mp;

        int prefix = 0;
        int count = 0;

        mp[0] = 1;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.size(); i++) {
            prefix += arr[i];

            if (mp.find(prefix - k) != mp.end()) {
                count += mp[prefix - k];
            }

            mp[prefix]++;
        }

        return count;
    }
};

